			"Message": "feat(Element): Sync submodule with layout/extension services and build config\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to deliver new workbench-tier Wind services and Mountain build config cleanup:\n- WorkbenchContextKeyService: Context key value management and expression evaluation\n- WorkbenchExtensionService: Extension activation and snapshot management\n- WorkbenchLayoutService: Workbench part visibility controls (ActivityBar, Sidebar, Panel, StatusBar)\n- WorkbenchProgressProblem: Problem ADT for progress task failures\n- Complete WorkbenchEditorService with Live implementation for pane management\n- Mountain: Revert production profile names to simple Mountain identifier, restore binary/library targets, update tauri.conf.json, remove duplicate externalBin entry, delete redundant backup files\n\nThis synchronization completes the workbench service surface expansion for VS Code integration while simplifying Mountain's build configuration.",
			"SHA": "041d0f106abd44a2f3e42876243da97ff54ec682"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:13:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add WorkbenchActivity and WorkbenchEditor services\n\nAdd two new workbench-tier Effect-TS service layers bridging VS Code's native activity and editor services to Wind's service architecture:\n\nWorkbenchActivityService:\n- Manages activity badges for view containers, views, accounts, and global activity\n- Provides ShowBadge (disposable badge with count/text/priority) and Clear operations\n- Problem ADT: WorkbenchActivityBridgeUnavailable, WorkbenchActivityRefused\n\nWorkbenchEditorService:\n- Bridges VS Code's native editor service for pane management\n- Provides Active (current editor snapshot), Open, CloseActive, and OnActiveChange stream\n- Open accepts resource URI with options for preserveFocus, preview, pinned, columnIndex\n- Problem ADT: WorkbenchEditorBridgeUnavailable, WorkbenchEditorOpenFailed, WorkbenchEditorCloseFailed\n\nBoth services follow the established Wind pattern with BridgeShape (upstream typed interface), Service (abstract contract), Tag (Context.Tag for DI), Problem (ADT for errors), and Live (runtime bridge implementation via globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES_).\n\nThis completes the workbench service surface expansion for VS Code integration.",
			"SHA": "cc839d3432a599cc5f04e8bbd5792207607fc7f4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:10:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add codegen emission layer for service schemas and catalog\n\nAdd the code emission layer to Wind's VS Code service codegen pipeline, completing Phase-2 of the system:\n- Codegen.ts: Runnable entry point invoked by prepublishOnly.sh\n- RunCodegen.ts: Orchestrator that walks source tree, extracts decorators, emits schemas\n- EmitServiceSchema.ts: Per-service schema emitter - writes <Decorator>Upstream.ts files with typed interface members and source-line back-links\n- EmitServiceCatalog.ts: Catalog emitter - writes ServiceCatalog.ts index of all discovered decorators with metadata\n- index.ts: Public exports for library consumers\n\nThe emission layer takes the ServiceDecoratorRecord extraction results from Phase-1 and produces typed TypeScript files under Effect/Generated/ that Wind bridge shapes can import type from. Schema files are idempotent (byte-identical on re-run) with diff-friendly formatting: members sorted by source line, JSDoc preserved verbatim.\n\nThis completes the codegen infrastructure for automated bridge shape generation from upstream VS Code source.",
			"SHA": "ef813840b80406694f4fab624f347e8b43f2072e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:08:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Element): Sync submodule with codegen pipeline and production build config\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Mountain: Update binary/lib names and Tauri config for production build profile. Rename the Mountain binary and library to include the full production environment profile string (ProductionNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_22NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Compile_ElectronProfile_EsbuildCompiler_Mountain) to distinguish this build variant from development builds. Update tauri.conf.json productName and identifier, and add Binary/node to externalBin for production node path.\n- Wind: Add VS Code service decorator codegen pipeline and global bridge accessor. Add a new regex-based codegen system that walks the VS Code source tree and extracts `createDecorator(...)` sites with interface members: ExtractDecoratorMatch, ExtractInterfaceMembers, IterateServiceDecorators, SourceTreeWalker. Also adds LandWorkbenchGlobal.ts - typed wrapper around globalThis.__CEL_WIND__ exposing CELWind().RunPromise(...) for Sky consumers.\n- Cocoon: Submodule pointer update.\n\nThis synchronization delivers the Wind codegen infrastructure for automated bridge shape generation from upstream VS Code source, while configuring Mountain for production build profile separation.",
			"SHA": "67e5c786563f61f9fb9a98555a3deacd073cb249"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:03:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add LandWorkbench composition layer and WorkbenchWorkspace service\n\nSynchronize Wind submodule to deliver a new LandWorkbench composition layer merging all previously-added workbench-tier services (Clipboard, Command, Dialog, Host, Keybinding, Lifecycle, Notification, Storage, Theme) plus the new WorkbenchWorkspace service into a single Layer for convenient consumption by Sky. The WorkbenchWorkspaceService bridges VS Code's native IWorkspaceService, providing Snapshot (workspace id, folders, configuration), Folders (array of workspace folders), FolderForResource (lookup folder by URI), and OnFolderChange (stream of folder add/remove/change events). The LandWorkbenchLayer uses Layer.mergeAll so a failure in one service doesn't poison others, and LandWorkbenchRuntime provides a lazy singleton ManagedRuntime for efficient per-webview instantiation.\n\nRefs: Land/.claude/tauri/Patches/14-StreamingGRPC.md",
			"SHA": "4b54c85e41012383576819cbcf9c5e792da6c05a"
		}
	],
